 :admission-note
 "All six are named in the mission's plan before implementation (cross-reference tables at mission :40-57, committed with the spec and the five futon3c patterns at futon3c 3dc50a81 2026-02-11) and re-attested by the closing implementation: five through code docstrings and call sites, loop-failure-signals through the typed transport-error call sites at ws.clj :123,:164,:181. None is recorded as drawn in during execution, so none is admitted. SEVEN OF THE THIRTEEN CROSS-REFERENCED PATTERNS ARE HONESTLY NOT NODES (corrected on reopen 2026-09-08: loop-failure-signals MOVES INTO the node set -- the closing ws.clj at 06dac238 implements typed transport errors at :123,:164,:181 -- and single-authority-registration MOVES OUT; see below): liveness-heartbeats and transport-pivot are marked '(future, not Part I-IV)' by the mission itself (:43,:44); reconnect-with-backoff is deferred ('the client's concern', :452); listener-leases is '(Part III cleanup)' and no lease/TTL code exists in ws.clj or ws/ (grep lease|ttl over both returns only unrelated 'release' matches); authoritative-transcript (:43) and single-line-transport (:47) name constraints, not implemented mechanisms, and no committed witness attests their involvement in the four completed parts; and SINGLE-AUTHORITY-REGISTRATION, though named in ws.clj:21's docstring, IS NOT IMPLEMENTED -- at the closing commit 06dac238 !connections is keyed by CHANNEL (the only guard is the unknown-channel defense at :123), the readiness path merely marks that channel connected, and no code rejects or evicts a second connection with the same agent-id; at the pinned f3534b93 the ws/invoke register! path still replaces the map entry with assoc rather than rejecting. A docstring naming a rule is not involvement; the first pass smoothed this and the reopen review caught it."
