 :rules
 [{:id :three-state-connection-lifecycle
   :member :realtime/connection-state-machine
   :then-source "futon3c/library/realtime/connection-state-machine.flexiarg:16"
   :interpretation-class :attested
   :interpretation
   "Implement a three-state machine (:connecting after open, :connected after first successful exchange, :disconnected after close), with pre-handshake failures ignored without cleanup."
   :attestation "futon3c/holes/missions/M-transport-adapters.md:52 (L2) and exit condition :486; src/futon3c/transport/ws.clj:4-6; mission commit 3dc50a81 authored the pattern beside the spec"
   :span-note "Content line only at pin f3534b93: marker :15, content :16."}
  {:id :require-readiness-handshake-before-processing
   :member :realtime/rendezvous-handshake
   :then-source "library/realtime/rendezvous-handshake.flexiarg:19"
   :interpretation-class :attested
   :interpretation
   "Connections must complete an explicit readiness handshake before any messages are processed; the implemented form is the WS ready event, not the full signed-hello exchange the THEN describes."
   :attestation "futon3c/holes/missions/M-transport-adapters.md:40 (R7 row 'WS readiness handshake before dispatch') and exit condition :484; src/futon3c/transport/ws.clj:10-11"
   :span-note "Content line only at futon3 pin ab277bdd: marker :18, content :19. NOTE: the mission's R7 wording ('readiness handshake before dispatch') is narrower than the THEN's signed-hello-with-capabilities form; the attestation covers the readiness reading, and the difference is stated here rather than smoothed."}
  {:id :three-tier-parameter-extraction
   :member :realtime/request-param-resilience
   :then-source "futon3c/library/realtime/request-param-resilience.flexiarg:16"
   :interpretation-class :attested
   :interpretation
   "Three-tier extraction (:query-string, then :request-uri parsing, then payload override) so no single library or proxy quirk loses the session identity."
   :attestation "futon3c/holes/missions/M-transport-adapters.md:54 (L1,L3 -- both lessons are transport-archaeology sections in the same mission, :59-70) and exit condition :487; src/futon3c/transport/ws.clj:178"
   :span-note "Content line only at pin f3534b93: marker :15, content :16."}
  {:id :surface-transport-failure-as-typed-error-frames
   :member :realtime/loop-failure-signals
   :then-source "library/realtime/loop-failure-signals.flexiarg:19"
   :interpretation-class :documented
   :interpretation
   "The implemented rule is narrower than the THEN's own terms: transport failures are surfaced to the sender as typed error frames at the layer that caused them (:unknown-connection, :not-ready, :invalid-frame), while the THEN text names sustained overload, rising drops, and JSONL stalls with tuning/backpressure as the response. The bridge is the mission's reading, not a claim the THEN states."
   :documentation "Class :documented per the commission's attested-or-documented rule, mirroring the M1 S1 treatment of the same pattern: the mission row (:48) and the closing code (ws.clj at 06dac238:123,164,181) attest the error-frame reading; no committed source attests that this reading of the THEN block is the pattern's own."
   :span-note "Content line only at futon3 pin ab277bdd: marker :18, content :19."}
